summary:
We're excited to share this new paper on the cover of #ACS Engineering Au, cover our work on multi-agent problem solving. In one example, using a set of seven LLM agents, each with specific expertise and capabilities, we can answer complex questions here: “Design molybdenene 2D materials by using ideas of flaw-tolerance in α-helical protein meshes. Develop three design principles that incorporate important mechanisms.” The agents collaborate to use data from the literature on molybdenene, protein meshes, and a book on multiscale modeling in their problem solving. Such agentic modeling can not only drive discovery by mining literature data, but can also generate its own, new data by invoking physics simulations. Paper:
