In our recent work we formulate scientific discovery as a representational phase transition (evidence can drive a system across an activation barrier into a new model class in which the same observations admit a much shorter description). @7uomok's work approaches biological organization from the complementary direction by asking how compact generative specifications produce organized living systems. Connecting these reveals a potential bridge between representation, information, kinetics, and physical thermodynamics all the way from how nature builds organized matter to how intelligence builds new explanations! 🚀
Quoting @7uomoki
@ProfBuehlerMIT Interestingly we found a similar(ish) connection between biological specification and statistical mechanics/ thermodynamics! I think there is lots to discover in the information-energy bridge in thermodynamics!
